# Source: HoareLogic.pdf, section "Exercises", "Single assignments", item 1.
id: assign-double
title: Doubling a variable
topic: Assignment
level: 1
source: HoareLogic.pdf, Exercises, "Single assignments" 1
tags: assignment, wp, consequence

task:
  Compute the weakest precondition with the assignment rule. Then check
  whether the given precondition implies it, and decide whether the
  triple is valid.

pre: x > 5
post: x > 10

program:
  {P}
  {R1}
  x := x * 2
  {Q}

verdict: valid

step: Apply the assignment rule
rule: ASSIGN, WP
focus: x := x * 2
text:
  The assignment rule replaces every occurrence of the assigned variable
  $x$ in the postcondition by the expression $x * 2$.
calc:
  wp(x := x * 2, Q)
  = (x > 10)[x <- x * 2]
  = x * 2 > 10
  = x > 5                 // divide both sides by 2
set: R1 = x > 5
text:
  The last line is an equivalence for integers: $2 * x > 10$ holds exactly
  when $x > 5$.

step: Compare with the precondition
rule: CONSEQUENCE, LOGIC
vc: x > 5 ==> x > 5
why:
  The weakest precondition is the precondition itself, and every formula
  implies itself.
result: The triple is valid.
